# Covers: SCHED-02 / B10 — host-C slot write between urbi_step calls
#         reaches a strand parked in waituntil(cond).
#
# Pre-fix: the pre-loop pump in urbi_step ran ISR-ring, ROS, periodics,
# and sleepers but NOT the reactive pipeline (slot-change drain +
# watcher-eval-dirty).  A host-C write that set the watched slot truthy
# bumped dirty_count, but with no strands runnable, the dispatch loop
# never executed and no safepoint ever drained it.  The parked waituntil
# strand was never woken.
#
# Fix (v0.13.3-scheduler-liveness, Task 5 — vm_reactive_drain):
# urbi_step now calls vm_reactive_drain when strand_runnable_count == 0
# BEFORE the dispatch loop.  The drain flushes the dirty mark, fires
# urbi_vm_watcher_eval_dirty, which sees the waituntil condition truthy and wakes
# the strand.  The subsequent dispatch loop runs the now-READY strand.
#
# Host-driver protocol:
#   1. run: install waituntil(Realm.go); on wake, set Realm.done = 42
#   2. step: drive to quiescent (strand parked in waituntil)
#   3. set-global go 1: simulate host-C write that sets go = 1
#   4. step: the idle-VM drain fires → waituntil wakes → strand runs
#   5. run: read Realm.done — must be 42

## host: run var Realm.go = false
## host: run waituntil(Realm.go); Realm.done = 42
## host: step 10000
## host: set-global go 1
## host: step 10000
## host: run Realm.done
[00000000] false
[00000000] nil
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] set-global: ok
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] 42
